    # - Firebase AI Connection

## - Firebase-specific setup
    Use the Firebase AI SDK and `google-services.json`. Hilt is optional; `ServiceLocator` or manual injection also works.

```kotlin
// app/src/main/java/com/codewithfk/expensetracker/android/ai/gateway/FirebaseAiGateway.kt
private val chatModel = Firebase.ai.generativeModel(modelName = modelName)

chatModel.generateContentStream(prompt).collect { chunk ->
    chunk.text?.let { emit(ChatResponse.Chunk(it)) }
}
```

## - Firebase operations
    Auth identifies users, Firestore stores chat data, and App Check protects requests. Retry, rate limits, and server-side cost controls still need explicit implementation.

